lib/IO/K8s/Role/Resource.pm:164-173 -- FROM_HASH is $class->new(%$hash)
with no inflation of nested objects. Every class has to_json, but
Pod->from_json($pod->to_json) dies at the first object-typed field with
a bare Moo type error on metadata that never points at the path that
works ($k8s->json_to_object / inflate).

Repro (measured): Pod JSON with metadata+spec dies with did not pass
type constraint "Maybe[InstanceOf[...ObjectMeta]]".

Loud, but an undocumented API asymmetry plus a diagnostics gap. Decide:
either document "flat classes only; use $k8s->json_to_object for nested
data" in POD, or route FROM_HASH through the registry inflation
(behaviour change, Changes entry). Note karr #53 (from_json utf8) sits
in the same method -- one pass can cover both.

Found in the 2026-08-18 core-module review (repro verified).
Lane: decision first, then io-k8s-worker or io-k8s-doc-writer.

Fixed: FROM_HASH routes through the registry inflation via a memoized default IO::K8s instance (require, not use -- a compile-time use would close a load cycle). Sound because _struct_to_object_expanded only ever sees pre-expanded class names. FROM_HASH inherits the karr #42 diagnostics; an undef on a required Bool now dies with 'Missing required arguments', converging with struct_to_object. Replaced the deliberate dies_ok assertion in t/24. Follow-up: IO::K8s::List is now the only class outside this symmetry (karr #64).
